# Cloud-side Log Ingestor (Fluent Bit aggregator) — dual-output alongside the
# direct Loki sink in fluent-bit.conf. Rendered by setup.sh from this template
# only when the Hub /api/edge/installer/v1/observability response provides both
# `log_ingest_endpoint` and `log_ingest_api_token`. Otherwise setup.sh writes
# an empty placeholder so the @INCLUDE in fluent-bit.conf still resolves.
#
# Wire / auth contract — dual-output log record contract, option C
# (AgenticSec docs/developer/system-design/technical-specs/log-ingestor.md):
#   - Edge ships the structured records verbatim as a JSON array (`Format
#     json`) to the Hub API Gateway, which performs native API Key auth on the
#     `x-api-key` header. The key is `{org_id}_{32-char hex}`; API Gateway VTL
#     strips the trailing 33 chars to recover `org_id` server-side and wraps the
#     body as `{"org_id": <recovered>, "records": <body>}` WITHOUT rebuilding it
#     (no field whitelist).
#   - The Cloud aggregator explodes that wrapper, stamps the authoritative
#     `org_id` and `env` onto every record, and dual-writes to Loki + CloudWatch.
#   - Because the body passes through unmodified, every field — `level` /
#     `run_id` / `supervisor_id` / `trace_id` / the free-form `app.details` —
#     reaches the aggregator intact. Edge does NOT pre-shape records and does
#     NOT inject `env`/`job`: the aggregator owns `env`, and `org_id` is
#     server-derived, so forgery is impossible.

[OUTPUT]
    Name              http
    Match             agenticsec.*
    Host              {{LOG_INGEST_HOST}}
    Port              443
    URI               {{LOG_INGEST_URI}}
    TLS               On
    TLS.verify        On
    Format            json
    # Records already carry `@timestamp`; disable the redundant epoch `date`
    # key the http output would otherwise inject.
    json_date_key     false
    Header            x-api-key {{LOG_INGEST_API_TOKEN}}
    storage.total_limit_size 1G
    Retry_Limit       no_limits
    net.dns.mode        UDP
    net.dns.resolver    LEGACY
    net.dns.prefer_ipv4 true
